<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Argentina's poverty rate climbs to nearly one in three under Milei</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24c1afcb4cd2817ec193c7dd92067dd10d61d5c0b7ab8e9e8474efc18569beb4</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T02:30:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-argentina-poverty-rate-nearly-one-in-three-milei" /><summary type="html">Argentina’s poverty rate rose to 32.3% in the first half of 2026 from 28.2% in the previous six months, official data showed on Thursday, as incomes lagged rising prices. Extreme poverty climbed to 7.5% from 6.3%. Among children aged 14 and under, 44.5% were poor.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Pope heads to France on first state visit in 18 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:064c39c2552771a3c1364239225306d242a08d894a4a4a638c0279f02550907f</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T01:57:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV flies to France on Friday for the Vatican's first state visit to the European nation in 18 years, with artificial intelligence and young believers near the top of his agenda. President Emmanuel Macron and his wife Brigitte will be on the tarmac to greet the 71-year-old pope.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal’s catastrophic floods were ‘warning to the world,’ PM Shah tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0348726852a9f3c2c13db02480986ea6feff0dad4ed37370d47ee4e8edf6b204</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T01:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260925-nepal-floods-warning-world-pm-shah-un" /><summary type="html">Nepal’s Prime Minister Balendra Shah said on Thursday that last month’s catastrophic floods were a “warning to the world” of growing climate risks in the Himalayas. He said warming was melting glaciers and permafrost and urged international support to help Nepal adapt to threats it could not face alone.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Live:  Iran's President says US ‘must choose’ whether to end war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70969280da32eee27d49597c6ab40e3118e68c6ecc3f8c7da975ecfbc3aaf5fe</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T23:52:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-live-iran-s-president-says-us-must-choose-whether-to-end-war" /><summary type="html">It is for the United States to choose whether to end its war in Iran as Tehran does not wish to continue fighting, Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian told Fox News in an interview aired Thursday. Pezeshkian took a defiant stand at the UN Wednesday, for which he travelled to New York, telling the world that Iran would not "bend at the knee" to Washington Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi reports fresh Houthi attacks as France pledges to defend key oil port</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdf5d0175b704572ba48b471ac97da4664f293dae878f95b8d7bdf3e7e041e8a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T23:34:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-saudi-houthi-attacks-france-oil-port" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia intercepted Houthi ballistic missiles on Thursday after warning several regions, including Mecca, of possible attacks. France said it would send military assets to help protect the Saudi oil terminal at Yanbu. The strikes came amid renewed fighting in Yemen that has killed dozens, according to sources cited by AFP.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump and Xi meet, but hopes for AI cooperation stay slim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab55373cd66766f66c388833fa1c7181031b9a632be921b9b84aaccd22d5248d</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T21:04:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-trump-and-xi-meet-but-hopes-for-ai-cooperation-stay-slim" /><summary type="html">Chinese President Xi Jinping and US President Donald Trump have been holding talks in the Oval Office at the White House today.  President Donald Trump gave the visiting leader of communist China a personal tour of several of his favorite White House features. He took him aboard the Marine One helicopter, presented the new granite landing pad he had built for it, and pointed out the massive adjacent construction site where a ballroom will eventually stand.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>‘Send in the Clowns’: Viral video fuels claims Denmark trolled Trump and Rubio</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66bd49cef87ccce9b531d50a3c1887b67befb9595ddcd68d737d9efd78003c7d</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T21:00:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/send-in-the-clowns-viral-video-fuels-claims-denmark-trolled-trump-and-rubio-1" /><summary type="html">A viral video claims Danish officials played Judy Collins’ “Send in the Clowns” as US Secretary of State Marco Rubio arrived for a Greenland signing ceremony, sparking claims of Danish “trolling”. Our checks of separate livestreams confirm the song really played and the video was not manipulated. Denmark has denied choosing the music, while the UN says it did not organise the event. Whilst the song was real, there is no evidence Denmark selected it deliberately. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Macron says 'CIA did not ​inform French services' of possible Russian drone attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f06810fbfbddd83c37eb2137dc17b6191cf9f834ed747c25801b5156b14d9d6</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T20:38:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260924-macron-says-cia-did-not-inform-french-services-of-possible-russian-drone-attacks" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday denied a report by Spanish newspaper El Mundo that the US Central Intelligence Agency had warned European governments of possible Russian drone attacks from the Mediterranean. He also said in a primetime TV interview that France will send troops and defence systems to Saudi Arabia to help protect the Red Sea port city of Yanbu.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Iran sees air, land travel chaos as US sanctions bite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:952149e9055dcb82cb5d0043cef0f8ab85b3d64412d10e0ee954ba3c4a0f2edf</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T20:35:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-air-land-travel-chaos-as-us-sanctions-bite" /><summary type="html">Flights between Iran and the United Arab Emirates have been suspended, following tighter US sanctions on Iran's aviation industry. The move effectively cuts Tehran off from Dubai, one of the region's most important commercial hubs. There are also huge backups near Iran's border with Turkey, as overland shipping routes struggle to fill the gaps. Also in this edition - Donald Trump and Xi Jinping hail strong ties between the US and China as they discuss AI, trade, and energy.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Tigray rebels in 'full-blown' war with government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc6ddb9637d40247af684ffd8a2a2a38504f8788f77d2f371c043cc1d130f702</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T20:23:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tigray-rebels-in-full-blown-war-with-government" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Tigrayans in northern Ethiopia start panic buying supplies in the rush to stock up amidst fears that months of tensions have  finally tipped over into full-blown conflict. Also, power cuts return to Senegal. And Yemis Alade, the Nigerian  superstar,  is out with a new album and speaks to   France 24.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli PM Netanyahu calls Gaza genocide allegations ‘biggest lie of the century’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bc31cb73aa0eb7353694c71b5e4ffe3f64cc5f1301c43c9df37a54a6e84b42f</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:31:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un--515acad11225.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gave a combative speech at the UN General Assembly on Thursday in which he denied that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza, lashed out at leaders, including New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani, and said attacking Iran was "one of the easiest decisions" he had ever made.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY:  Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu speaks at the UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08c45718f7c55bb43d6277b2f021e4d2bd76bb71e30a10823201e831bad79a79</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:28:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-israeli-prime-minister-benjamin-netanyahu-speaks-at-the-unga--1b234a422e53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-israeli-prime-minister-benjamin-netanyahu-speaks-at-the-unga" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on ​Thursday mounted a forceful defense of Israel's actions in the region at the UN, seeking to counter growing international isolation ahead of elections he could lose, as dozens of delegates streamed out.</summary></entry><entry><title>The future of AI in their hands? Trump-Xi summit dismisses calls for global oversight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ea5aad64f464b1b075a8133cff9087f544dd3875d14a2d20d5abbde78434ae0</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:05:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260924-the-future-of-ai-in-their-hands-trump-xi-summit-dismisses-calls-for-global-oversight--3fbc99bf55eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260924-the-future-of-ai-in-their-hands-trump-xi-summit-dismisses-calls-for-global-oversight" /><summary type="html">It’s their AI world and we’re just living in it. If that's the feeling of those who suffer from AI anxiety, it may worsen watching the Chinese president’s first state visit to Washington in nine years. If there's one issue where the planet's biggest superpowers agree on, it's now’s not the time for global regulation of artificial intelligence. As they sit down to a White House dinner hours after news that OpenAI had hacked the Australian government, we’ll ask who will call to task the US tech titans at the table.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Residents in West Bank's Masafer Yatta face Israeli demolitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a3c56ac2131916ed9cb5d197a5ede4918fea74d87c945af791ed08a5948f811</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:47:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions--70cf9dfea7fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions" /><summary type="html">On September 2, the Israeli army demolished the village of Khirbet a-Taban in the occupied West Bank. The village is located in Masafer Yatta, an area Israel declared a restricted military zone. Residents of the area have been reporting an increase in demolitions by the Israeli army and harassment by Israeli settlers since the October 7 Hamas attack.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: ‘We’re going to win because we’ve got no other choice’, Israeli PM Netanyahu says at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eeef6dd0ffa3cd1cb5c7b7a0a25b66c5f9aef51d23d5d38befb6a8c560c159c5</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:18:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video--ff8dcde9286d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli policies threaten 'life and existence' of Palestinians, Abbas tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3f63e18f91529475d196de7b82e0556509d140d745a52de2f437dd929d1973a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un--ab406195501e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un" /><summary type="html">Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas addressed the UN General Assembly on Thursday by video after being denied a visa to the United States for the second year in a row. In his prerecorded speech, he denounced Israeli policies that he said threatened Palestinians with a new Nakba and vowed that his people would remain “on their land”.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Schism with rebel Catholic sect casts a pall over Pope Leo’s visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:990b541dd3d4003633f32879c64a06347c4a6ca32af674da03ef8ce42a2529b3</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:18:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes--83fe705c42fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes" /><summary type="html">The Vatican’s recent excommunication of followers of a Catholic splinter sect, the Society of Saint Pius X, has revived a longstanding feud within the Roman Catholic Church ahead of Pope Leo XIV’s state visit to France. The ultra-conservative group has established an extensive network of schools and has attracted thousands of followers in France.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Threat to 'life and existence': Major takeaways from Palestinian president's UN speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc8ac251bdafe32525eb690152cb3c0222cafa911b732e8395a266601c054883</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:09:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-threat-to-life-and-existence-major-takeaways-from-palestinian-president-s-un-speech--c71b8c10de4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-threat-to-life-and-existence-major-takeaways-from-palestinian-president-s-un-speech" /><summary type="html">Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas addressed the UN General Assembly on Thursday, delivering prerecorded remarks from his office in Ramallah after the United States denied him and other top Palestinian officials visas to attend the gathering for the second year in a row. “The Palestinian people face one of the most dangerous times in its history,” Abbas said. France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani takes a look at some of the main takeaways from his address.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Palestinian president Abbas addresses UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcd10088a1dc415e828aa7a8055132aa3a2ae761cb27378d188b2fa85318f165</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:06:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-palestinian-president-abbas-addresses-un-general-assembly--2776060765d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-palestinian-president-abbas-addresses-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">Palestinian president Mahmud Abbas told the UN on Thursday that Israeli policies no longer just jeopardized a two-state solution but were now threatening the "very life and existence" of his people. Abbas delivered prerecorded remarks to the UN’s General Assembly from his office in Ramallah after the United States denied him and other top Palestinian officials visas to attend the gathering for the second year in a row.</summary></entry><entry><title>How do the French feel about religion?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d16b0479ecfef3485bb130a6d141e8ec9a50e5f00a90e1e6e7e1afd3541a667</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:03:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260924-how-do-the-french-feel-about-religion--05e8eabc636a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260924-how-do-the-french-feel-about-religion" /><summary type="html">Amid the enthusiasm over the first papal visit to France in 18 years, we take a deep dive into religion in France. We try to answer the question, "How do the French feel about religion?" From its Catholic heritage to laïcité, or secularism, we break down the statistics on the French people's relationship to faith.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37d73f5a92936928222374e834c2fa2158b5ddf1f3263e3bfab363fd8e5b819a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed--29eaaa0e21d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan.</summary></entry><entry><title>United States: Trump's unconventional welcome for Xi's state visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cad85a65438a37cacbf9885c430c7e20a9a43f529b513baa55925b5b68d88427</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:40:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-united-states-trump-s-unconventional-welcome-for-xi-s-state-visit--138f04a14989.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-united-states-trump-s-unconventional-welcome-for-xi-s-state-visit" /><summary type="html">🇺🇸 🇨🇳 In a first for a US president, Donald Trump greeted his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping on the tarmac as the latter landed in a military airbase near Washington DC on Wednesday for a three-day state visit.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Palestinian President Abbas calls on UN General Assembly to 'not allow another Nakba'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efb634860451442872a5d47d0fcf6d9e79af80363d4eeaf663be4f1fea2b2443</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:29:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video--ff8dcde9286d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video" /></entry><entry><title>Nigerian superstar Yemi Alade: From viral hit 'Johnny' to working with Beyoncé</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4272d3942bb8f021361e6bfdc929bf5347952920ab2d4bdbe2eba7bf8e9c86d5</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:16:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260924-nigerian-superstar-yemi-alade-from-viral-hit-johnny-to-working-with-beyonc--4070c723efb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260924-nigerian-superstar-yemi-alade-from-viral-hit-johnny-to-working-with-beyonc%C3%A9" /><summary type="html">Nigerian superstar Yemi Alade is one of Africa's biggest female artists, with global hits, hundreds of millions of views online and a collaboration with Beyoncé. Speaking to Eve Jackson as she kicks off her new tour, the Grammy-nominated singer looks back on her remarkable career, reveals how she nearly missed the email that led to her "Black Is King" collaboration with Beyoncé and talks about her new album, "It's Yemi Alade", and latest single "Ala Bekee" with Don Jazzy.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry></feed>
